# The Required rule of the same name holds every other restatement.
# `In short,` and `Ultimately,` sit here, because each also leads a
# point the paragraph has not made yet (`Ultimately, your applications
# run as containers inside Pods`). Each counts only with the glued
# comma of an opener, since mid-sentence `ultimately` places a step
# last (`the request ultimately reaches the scheduler`).
expr main [(in short,), (ultimately,)]
let message "Restatement. Make the first statement stand alone, and delete the phrase."
let description "Flags `in short` and `ultimately` as sentence openers that announce a summary."
let becomes ""
let kind "Style"
let scope "Sentence"
allows "The request ultimately reaches the scheduler."
